---
SCALE PROBES (product host — `/tmp/s71_peer2`)
---

Hang budget = **10s** (`timeout`). Dual-repro where noted.

### Long arg lists (`println(a0, …, aN-1)` + N lets)
| N | tokens | check | emit-c (10s) | emit-c (30s) |
|---|--------|-------|--------------|--------------|
| 50 | 0.06–0.13s | 1.03s | **0.42–1.37s PASS** dual | — |
| 200 | 1.23s | **12.93s** rss 250 MB | **HANG/TERM 10s** | **10.85s** rss 135 MB |
| 500 | — | — | TERM 10s | — |
| 1000 | — | — | TERM 10s | — |

**Attribution:** `check` does **not** call `c_guard_scan_idents`.
check(200) > emit-c(200) ⇒ cost is typecheck / env / check-path secret
walk, not the 7.1 emit walker. args string for N=200 is ~1–2 KiB;
linear slice scan cannot explain 10s.

### Long ident names (`let xaaa… = 1; println(xaaa…)`)
| L | tokens | check | emit-c |
|---|--------|-------|--------|
| 256 | 0.08s | 0.11s | **0.13–0.39s PASS** dual |
| 1024 | 0.17s | 0.45s | **0.46–0.83s PASS** dual |
| 4096 | 0.50–0.93s | 9.09s | **5.91–8.39s PASS** (tight) |
| 16384 | **7.46s** | (not finished in 10s budget) | **HANG 10s** |
| 65536 | — | — | **ERR load 64KiB per-file** (honest) |

**Attribution:** `try_scan_ident` (`token_scan_ident.oo:28`)
`id = id + c2` per character — O(L²) lexer. tokens(16384)=7.46s already
eats most of the 10s budget before emit guard runs.

### Fail rail (correctness + no hang)
| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `// SECRET: tok…` L=256 + `println(tok…)` | rc=1 `ERR	secret	println sink refuses SECRET tok…` **0.08–0.16s** dual **PASS** |
| 500 args, last SECRET | 10s timeout — **no refuse witness** (pipeline, not FN proof) |

### Combo
200 idents × 64 chars: emit-c TERM at 10s — same class as N=200 + long names.

