or document.*

| Layer | Fixed? | In host? |
|-------|--------|----------|
| 7.1 `str_slice` walker | yes (HEAD L105) | **yes** (objdump + stage1 C) |
| WT `__sec_sink__` emit_guard | WT-only, not 7.1 concat | **no** — host predates; **not** a 7.1 leak |

**Document, do not REJECT 7.1:** host is current for the slice body;
stale only vs concurrent WT `__sec_sink__` (2.10-class wrapper). A later
pure-multi rebuild should pick that up; this peer did **not** rebuild.

Do **not** use `oodac_bin` (Aug 11, 908632 B) as product host.

---
RESIDUALS (honest, out of 7.1 close)
---

1. **Lexer ident concat** — `token_scan_ident.oo` `id = id + c2`. Dominates
   L≥4k–16k. Not 7.1.
2. **Check/emit scale** — N=200 `println` ~11–13s, 135–250 MB. Not the
   ident walker (check path).
3. **7.10** — `c_parse_secret_env` still `name = name + c`.
4. **7.2** — sibling last-arg slice; not re-proved here.
5. **Letter-class giant `||`** — O(62) `str_eq` per char in the walker.
   Linear factor, not quadratic concat. Residual cost only.
6. **64KiB per-file load cap** — L=65536 never reaches the walker.

## WHAT THIS PEER WILL NOT RUBBER-STAMP
- Peer1 ACCEPT of **scan contract** (IDENT refuse / string FP) — not
  re-litigated; different OWN. See `s71_peer1.oot`.
- Rollup “path-A closed including scale no-hang.”
- Any claim that 10s no-hang holds for N=200 or L=16k on product host.

